  "description": "A parametric KITCHEN COUNTER on the six-node spine — Geometry → Input Properties → Math Engine → Output Metrics → 2D Render + 3D Render.\n\nSEGMENT-HOSTED, and that is the point. Drop it on a wall and the host frame takes the wall's direction and length; set Fit to host to Exact and the run fills the wall exactly, with the back of the counter on the wall face. A counter is the one kitchen object whose length is never typed — it is whatever the wall is.\n\nTHE UNITS ARE COUNTED, NOT DRAWN. \"Auto\" divides the run by 600 mm and rounds, clamped to 1..12, so a 2.4 m run gives four fronts and a 3.1 m run gives five without anyone editing a list; the fixed options override it when a real kitchen has a real unit schedule. The fronts are built in a bounded loop that accumulates quad rows — the only loop in this object, and the reason the count can be a parameter at all.\n\nFIVE PIECES, FIVE SLOTS — worktop, carcass, toe kick, splashback, fronts. The toe kick is set back from the front face rather than being a shorter carcass, which is what makes the plan read as cabinetry and the 3D show a real recess.\n\nSTORAGE VOLUME is published net of the toe recess and the worktop, because the useful number is what fits in the cupboards, not the box the cupboards occupy.",
